            <ArticleTitle>Latent plaque rupture in a patient undergoing stenting for acute coronary syndrome and diffuse coronary disease: a case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>241-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Secondary prevention of plaque rupture following percutaneous coronary intervention in patients with acute coronary syndrome is not well studied. This case report describes a 53-year-old man who experienced plaque rupture between two previously successfully implanted stents in the right coronary artery, as documented during the 3rd intervention using intravascular ultrasound.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2006 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
